2. Code decompiled from MT Manager (`patch/src/main/java/bin/`)
---------------------------------------------------------------

  * `bin/mt/apksign/` (`data/`, `key/` included) — APK Signature Scheme v2/v3 signing:
    builds the APK Signing Block and inserts it in place.
  * `bin/zip/` — ZIP reading and writing: `DataMultiplexing` implements the
    "original-APK data multiplexing" the patch pipeline relies on (a patched APK keeps
    the untouched original APK inside it, and the entries copied from it share that data
    area instead of being duplicated), plus streaming signatures and alignment.
  * `bin/io/` — random-access helpers used by the two packages above.

  Every file in these three packages carries its original `@author Bin` header. They are
  decompiled from **MT Manager** (MT管理器) <https://mt2.cn>. **We could not find license
  terms for this code.** It is kept because the patch pipeline depends on it: `bin.zip`
  is what makes a patched app cost one copy of the original APK instead of two, and
  `bin.mt.apksign` is the only signer we found that can sign such a multiplexed archive
  in place — Google's apksig rewrites every entry, which duplicates the multiplexed data
  and roughly doubles the artefact (measured on a synthetic multiplexed APK:
  11 983 321 B → 23 725 457 B, against 11 990 608 B when signed by `bin.mt.apksign`).
  If you own the rights to this code and object to its redistribution here, open an
  issue and it will be removed.


